2. THE DECIDING PIN RESTATED ON THE READ k_a(6): alpha from the arrival Nodes over k from the lamp, both clicks
   the run's 0.731 Links = 26 x C_nodes x k_cont(6): 26 x 2.496 x 0.01127 = 0.731 (k_cont the continuum's 3 q n / (4 pi d b) at q = 4640, the one GAMEBOARD input of the chain)
   alpha_nodes = 0.731 / 26 = 0.02812 radians (DETECTOR, the arrival Nodes' mean over 40 starts; the bracket 0.00096)
   alpha_nodes / k_ring (the 40 lamps' mean) = 0.02812 / 0.02285 = 1.230; through the lever-arm factor 0.683 the constant 1.801 (the run's C_ring 3.655 on k_cont), against 2 c_f = 4 on the comparison side
   alpha_nodes / k_shell (the 3D shell) = 0.02812 / 0.01120 = 2.510; through the lever-arm factor 0.683 the constant 3.675 (the run's C_ring 3.655 on k_cont), against 2 c_f = 4 on the comparison side
   alpha_nodes / k_cont = 0.02812 / 0.01127 = 2.495; through the lever-arm factor 0.683 the constant 3.653 (the run's C_ring 3.655 on k_cont), against 2 c_f = 4 on the comparison side
   THE PIN: the ring of lamps at b = 6 reads the mean count ratio 1 + k with k = 0.02285 (the algebra's, DETECTOR when read), the bracket 3.4 percent of itself (0.025 / 0.731, the ring's own) beyond the reading's grain of section 1; the 0.731 +- 0.025 restated: alpha_nodes = 1.230 x k_read within the same bracket, i.e. the ratio of the two clicks 1.230 +- 0.084 (both brackets); FAIL if the read k departs from 0.02285 by more than the bracket, or the ratio of clicks leaves its bracket

